# Allowlist .gitignore for the PUBLIC repo.
#
# Policy: everything is ignored by default. Code and build docs are allowed
# back in explicitly. Hard blocks are listed LAST so they win over the allows
# (git applies the last matching rule).
#
# Never in this repo: credentials, any data tier or cache, results / reports /
# figures, research verdict documents, the ledger, and live watchlist configs.
# See RECOVERY.md for what lives in the private mirror instead.

# ── default-deny ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*
!*/

# ── allowed code + config extensions ─────────────────────────────────────
!*.py
!*.yaml
!*.yml
!*.toml
!*.cfg
!*.ini
!*.js
!*.css
!*.html
!.gitignore
!.env.example

# ── docs: allow-listed by exact path (research findings stay private) ────
!/README.md
!/RECOVERY.md
!/EARNINGS_VOL_PROGRAM_PLAN.md
!/guides/*.md
!/engine/**/*.md
!/checks/*.md
!/tests/*.md
!/tools/*.md
!/tools/opencode_config.json
!/tools/opencode_review_config.json

# ── ui/ (React/TypeScript client): narrow explicit allowlist ─────────────
# TypeScript and JSON are not allowed globally above (only py/yaml/toml/
# js/css/html/...) — Phase 3 guide §7: "Add exact source/config/lockfile
# allowlist rules for ui/ before existing hard blocks. Do not allow JSON or
# TypeScript globally." Listed by exact path/extension under ui/ only, so a
# stray .ts or .json anywhere else in the repo stays blocked by the
# default-deny, and nothing under ui/ rides in on a directory wildcard.
!/ui/package.json
!/ui/package-lock.json
!/ui/tsconfig.json
!/ui/tsconfig.*.json
!/ui/vite.config.ts
!/ui/index.html
!/ui/README.md
!/ui/.gitignore
!/ui/src/**/*.ts
!/ui/src/**/*.tsx
!/ui/src/**/*.css

# ── ops/ (systemd units for the native nightly trigger) ──────────────────
# The trigger's units are operational config that must ship with the code
# (dashboard/README.md documents the install). .service/.timer are neither
# allowed extensions nor docs, so the default-deny blocks them without an
# explicit allowlist. Exact paths/extensions under ops/ only, so nothing else
# under it can ride in.
!ops/
!ops/systemd/
!ops/systemd/*.service
!ops/systemd/*.timer

# ── HARD BLOCKS (last rule wins — these override every allow above) ──────

# credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Loose exploratory scripts at the repo root: pre-engine research, with
# findings embedded in comments and hardcoded result values. Code, but not
# code this repo publishes — they go to the private mirror.
/*.py

# One-off instrumented/diagnostic harnesses (RSS probes, monkeypatched
# capture re-runs, etc.). Useful on disk for the run that needed them, never
# meant to be a maintained tool — 7952363 tracked one on capture-retention by
# accident (the `!*.py` allow above puts every .py back in, scratch/ included,
# unless blocked here). Stays untracked; keep on disk locally as needed.
/scratch/

# AGENTS.md carries the user's oquants account workspace/model IDs and the
# decoded coefficients of a paid vendor's model. Operational and binding, but
# private.
/AGENTS.md

# dashboard/shared.py hardcodes the thesis watchlist universe. That is position
# intent, which never ships publicly — the guide names the same content as
# off-limits when it lives in config/thesis/universe.yaml, and it is no more
# publishable for being embedded in a module. Revisit when Phase 3 moves the
# universe into config.
# Written as `/dashboard/*` rather than `/dashboard/`: git does not descend into
# an excluded DIRECTORY, so a `!` rule under one is silently dead. Excluding the
# entries instead keeps the two exceptions below working — and keeps every
# subdirectory (cache/, earnings/, published/) excluded and undescended, which
# is what holds the rendered bundle's licensed quotes and position intent out of
# a public remote.
/dashboard/*
# Two exceptions, both pure code/docs carrying no universe and no market data:
# the Phase 3 board's server, and the directory's README (how to run both
# dashboards, plus the Cloudflare Access checklist).
!/dashboard/README.md
!/dashboard/earnings_app.py

# data tiers, caches, and the grandfathered research trees
/data/
/ledger/
/reports/
/polygon_cache/
/earnings_predictions/
/bt/
/config/thesis/
**/results/
**/figures/
**/models/
**/cache/
**/__pycache__/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# ui/ dependencies and build output: large, generated, reproducible from
# ui/package.json + ui/package-lock.json. Must be a HARD block, not just an
# absence from the allow list above: node_modules/dist are full of .js/.css
# files, which ARE allowed globally by the extension rules above, so without
# this the directory-wildcard `!*/` plus `!*.js` would let them back in.
/ui/node_modules/
/ui/dist/

# data + artifact file types (defence in depth behind the extension allowlist)
*.csv
*.csv.gz
*.tsv
*.parquet
*.json.gz
*.jsonl
*.gz
*.zip
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.joblib
*.h5
*.npy
*.npz
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.pdf
*.log
*.done*

# ── re-includes that must outrank the hard blocks above ──────────────────

# `**/models/` above exists to keep the grandfathered research model trees out.
# engine/models/ is not one of those: it holds the registry loader, the training
# scripts, and the registry manifest — all code and config, all public. The
# trained artifacts it describes live in data/models/, which stays blocked by
# the /data/ rule, by the .joblib suffix, and by checks/repo_hygiene.py.
!/engine/models/
!/engine/models/**/
!/engine/models/**/*.py
!/engine/models/registry.json
# Which SHAPE each structure family trades. Same kind of thing as the
# registry manifest and public for the same reason: a clone without it
# silently falls back to the incumbent champion, so the code would run a
# structure nobody chose while reporting success.
!/engine/models/structures.json

# `**/models/` above blocks the grandfathered research model trees. The v2
# model packages are not one of those: they are the empty skeleton of
# system_rearchitecture.md §4.4's layer-3 inference package and its layer-6
# training package, code and READMEs only. Same reason /engine/models/ is
# re-included above; a separate rule because git matched the block, not the
# allow, for every path under it.
!/engine/v2/models/
!/engine/v2/models/**/

# The migration's progress meter (system_rearchitecture.md §4.6): every
# engine/v2 -> legacy dependency, with a reason and a date, plus the committed
# count that may only shrink. Config, not data — and a clone without it cannot
# run `checks/import_layers.py` at all, which is the check that keeps the two
# trees apart.
!/checks/legacy_adapters.json

# The versioned pre-commit hook. Extensionless, so the default-deny above
# catches it; and the whole point of checks/hooks/ is that .git/hooks is NOT
# versioned, so a clone with no copy of this file has no gate at all.
!/checks/hooks/pre-commit

# The environment lock. Code-adjacent config, and the thing that lets a clean
# checkout reproduce the baseline the tier-0 corpus was captured in.
!/requirements.txt
!/ruff.toml

# Test-runner tooling pins that must NOT be gated with requirements.txt --
# see requirements-dev.txt's own header for why it is separate.
!/requirements-dev.txt
!/checks/v2_coverage_ratchet_phase1_baseline.json
!/checks/v2_coverage_ratchet_phase2_baseline.json
!/checks/mutation_ratchet_baseline.json

# The Phase 2 acceptance registry (phase-2 guide §12.1): which tests and,
# for tier-2 rows, which Phase2Evidence fields prove each D01-D20 row.
# Config, not data or evidence — the gate reads it to know what to check.
!/checks/phase2_acceptance.json

# The Phase 3 acceptance registry (phase-3 guide §10): which Phase3Evidence
# comparison-receipt kinds / negative-control kinds / single fields prove
# each L01-L14 row. Config, not data or evidence.
!/checks/phase3_acceptance.json

# The reviewed legacy->v2 table-contract mapping's per-column facts (unit,
# scale, sentinel/null policy, etc.) that engine/data/schemas.py itself does
# not declare (phase-2 guide §5.1, §12 D02). Config/review data, not licensed
# rows: no ticker, price, or quote ever appears here, only column-shape facts
# quoted from Column.doc/CONVENTIONS/SOURCE_PRIORITY. Same reason as the two
# re-includes above — engine/v2/data/legacy_adapter.py cannot build a mapping
# from a clone without it.
!/engine/v2/data/legacy_annotations.json

# Claude Code state, entirely. `settings.local.json` alone was not enough: the
# default-deny above re-allows directories (`!*/`) and then every `.py`, so a
# git WORKTREE checked out under .claude/ — which is where Claude Code puts
# them — has its whole source tree swept back in. Found 2026-09-05 with an 18MB
# `.claude/worktrees/tier4-build` staged for commit by `git add .`.
#
# This is the general hole, not one stray directory: any nested checkout under
# an allowed directory inherits the code allowances. Blocking the tool's own
# state directory closes the case that actually occurs.
.claude/

# Mutation-testing pilot (tools/mutation_pilot.py). Its state lives OUTSIDE the
# repo, in ~/.cache/investing-plan-mutation-pilot/<module>/. These rules only
# catch an accidental `mutmut run` from the checkout: mutmut writes a mutated
# copy of engine/ to ./mutants/, whose .py files the code allowances above
# would otherwise sweep back in.
mutants/
.mutmut-cache
mutmut-stats.json
mutmut-debug.log
